@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
hide empty description
title Event lifecycle and save boundaries

state NOT_STARTED
state WAITING
state ACCEPTING_ANSWER
state RESOLVING
state COMPLETED

[*] --> NOT_STARTED
NOT_STARTED --> WAITING : prepareEvent(...)\n[reaction]
NOT_STARTED --> ACCEPTING_ANSWER : prepareEvent(...)\n[puzzle or dialogue]
WAITING --> ACCEPTING_ANSWER : updateEvent(...)\n[delay elapsed]
ACCEPTING_ANSWER --> RESOLVING : submitAnswer(...)
RESOLVING --> ACCEPTING_ANSWER : [dialogue opening]\nprepareFollowUp(...)
RESOLVING --> COMPLETED : completeEvent()\n[terminal response resolved]
COMPLETED --> [*]

note left of WAITING
  Reaction delay only.
  Both input modes poll it.
end note
note right of ACCEPTING_ANSWER
  Controller owns the clock.
  Overdue input is incorrect.
  Resume keeps this stage
  with a fresh deadline.
end note
note right of RESOLVING
  Effects cannot be saved midway
  or reward twice on retry.
end note
legend bottom
  States are EventEncounter.EventPhase values.
  NOT_STARTED, WAITING and ACCEPTING_ANSWER are saveable.
  Only a dialogue opening creates another answer stage.
  Inline validation, UI calls and failure paths are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
